r to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 23 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186311921 :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $w=⟨4,7,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-33i+13j-41k \\\\  & =⟨-33,13,-41⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-33,13,-41⟩.$" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $w=⟨4,7,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-33i+13j-41k \\\\  & =⟨-33,13,-41⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-33,13,-41⟩.$"] [:db/cas 17592186311922 :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨3,-9,-5⟩$ and $w=⟨-8,9,3⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -9 & -5 \\\\ -8 & 9 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =18i+31j-45k \\\\  & =⟨18,31,-45⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨18,31,-45⟩.$" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨3,-9,-5⟩$ and $w=⟨-8,9,3⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -9 & -5 \\\\ -8 & 9 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =18i+31j-45k \\\\  & =⟨18,31,-45⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨18,31,-45⟩.$"] [:db/cas 17592186311923 :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186311923 :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-5,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,1,-2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-3i-7j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.$" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-5,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,1,-2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ 